abstract: "The complete Obsidian vault of the CRG-Flux framework: a cross-scale bridge from local flexoelectric deformations in 2D lattices (graphene wrinkling, tip-effect enhancement, yield-threshold switching) to stationary-action closures in pre-Friedmann geometry. Nineteen canonical notes across seven sections with a Routh-Hurwitz attractor proof (bistability honestly registered), the family-register mapping to LIMEN/SPUMA, and a figure/asset provenance register. Model-level claims with executed numerical protocols; no empirical cosmological claim is made."
